1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Landhandlare, Cand. Theol.; Ringsaker's first 'Ordfører' (1837-39) and the last 'Landkremmeren' (owner) of Stein Farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henrik Steen is said to have been a pattern for the character Hans Orre in Tryggve Andersen's book: "I Cancelliraadens Dage" (In the Days of the Councillor) first published in Norway in 1897 and later translated into English.  The
2 CONC  book is an historical novel in the form of a set of short stories about life on and near the Stein (aka Steen, Steyn) Farm in Ringsaker on lake Mjøsa between Hamar and Lillehammer.
2 CONT
2 CONT matriculated and studied theology at Copenhagen. Later took over Stein farm and the merchant business. He became an atheist and a republican influenced by the literary trends in Europe at the time. He became chairman of the county
2 CONC  council around 1837 in Ringsaker.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was close to Bankrupcy when he died in 1869. His son Johan Wilhelm Emmigrated with his family and the Stein farm was sold at Auction in 1870.  The farm burnt down in 1897 and very different buildings are there today.
2 CONT
2 CONT source: Njaul Pharo
